        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "All work is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## What I built\n\nA real INI parser + printer for this repo's dialect, in MoonBit, split by responsibility:\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ini.mbt` | `parse`: single-pass line loop, document assembly, section re-opening / last-wins |\n| `ini_lines.mbt` | physical line splitting (LF/CRLF, `splitlines` semantics) |\n| `ini_chars.mbt` | char classes, trimming, range helpers |\n| `ini_section.mbt` | `[name]` recognition, quote-pair stripping, bracket/empty rejection |\n| `ini_entry.mbt` | key/value split at the **first** `=`/`:`, key validation (control chars, emptiness) |\n| `ini_value.mbt` | quoted carriers with per-carrier escape sets, quote scanning, inline comments, backslash continuation (raw-run parity) |\n| `ini_printer.mbt` | `print` with quote-on-demand carriers so `parse(print(doc)) == doc` |\n| `ini_errors.mbt` | `IniError.Malformed(message)` |\n\nLines are materialized as `Array[Char]` so every index is a plain `Int` over one representation — no mixing of UTF-16 code-unit and code-point offsets (the usual source of panics around surrogate pairs).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `moon test` → **61/61 pass** (the 12 public tests plus 49 I added: spec-derived valid/invalid suites, printer round-trips for hostile values, and a 1000-document quickcheck round-trip stress run).\n- `moon check` → exit 0, no diagnostics from my files (the only remaining warning is `test_unqualified_package` inside the provided `ini_pub_test.mbt`, which must not be modified).\n- `moon fmt` applied; `pkg.generated.mbti` is current and lists `parse`, `print`, `Doc` and `pub suberror IniError`.\n- Two independent audits (spec compliance, crash/edge-case hunt). The audit found one genuine defect — a section name that is itself one quote pair (`[\"\"a\"\"]` → name `\"a\"`) printed back as `[\"a\"]` and lost the pair. Fixed in `encode_section_name` (`wrapped_in_quote`) with regression tests; also hardened `starts_comment` against out-of-range indices.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- `moon info` itself could not be executed: the tool sandbox refuses that spawn (it writes `.mbti` sources). The interface file was nevertheless regenerated by the toolchain during `moon fmt`/`moon check` and correctly reflects the added error type.\n- Where `specs/ini.md` is genuinely open I picked and documented a reading in `README.md` (`## Design decisions`, `## Limits`): a continuation marker immediately before EOF is an error (a final line break is not a line), continuation lines contribute verbatim text, whitespace is trimmed on raw text before escape decoding, and `print` cannot round-trip keys/names the dialect itself cannot spell (empty keys, separators or comment markers in keys, brackets in section names)."
        }
