        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a general INI parser in MoonBit for this repo's dialect, plus a printer whose output round-trips.\n\n## What was built (root `ini` package, one file per responsibility)\n\n| File | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| `scanner.mbt` | whitespace/control-char predicates, CRLF-aware line splitting, trailing-backslash counting |\n| `value.mbt` | `Carrier` enum (unquoted / `\"...\"` / `'...'`), per-carrier escape decoding, inline-comment cutting, quoted-value scanning, continuation joining |\n| `parser.mbt` | section-header parsing, key validation, entry parsing, document assembly (`parse`) |\n| `printer.mbt` | value escaping and header rendering (`print`) |\n| `error.mbt` | single error path (`ini: line N: <rule>`) and the control-character predicate |\n| `README.md` | overview, architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, design decisions, limits |\n\nKey rules implemented: LF/CRLF lines with no phantom trailing line; `;`/`#` full-line and whitespace-preceded inline comments; `[name]` headers with quote stripping, bracket rejection and re-open/last-wins; first `=` or `:` as separator; key trimming with empty/control-character rejection; quoted values that must close on their own line and may be followed only by whitespace or a comment; the per-carrier escape table (`\\n \\r \\t \\\\ \\\" \\'` and \"as written\" fallback); continuation by the **parity** of the trailing backslash run, decided before escape processing, with continuation lines appended verbatim as text; `print` always double-quoting values and quoting section names only when needed.\n\n## Validation (commands actually run)\n\n- `moon test` → **92/92 pass** (12 given public cases incl. both quickcheck properties, 72 rule-derived edge cases, 7 real-world sample/round-trip cases, 1 brute-force fuzz over ~64 000 hostile strings).\n- `moon check` → 0 errors; 3 warnings, all in files the task forbids editing (`ini_pub_test.mbt` unqualified `Doc`, `ini_spec.mbt` deprecated `derive(...)`) plus a pre-existing test-only import in `moon.pkg`. Every file I added is warning-free.\n- `moon fmt` run (and its rewrite of the protected `ini_spec.mbt` reverted — that file is byte-for-byte the original; `moon fmt --check` therefore reports only it). `pkg.generated.mbti` regenerated by `moon check` and matches the required API exactly: `pub fn parse(StringView) -> Doc raise`, `pub fn print(Doc) -> String`, no extra public items.\n\n## Independent audits\n\nTwo review-subagent audits against `specs/ini.md` ran; the first found three real divergences, which I fixed and covered with tests: (1) inline comments were cut from the *joined* continuation value instead of only the first physical line (spec: a continuation line's comment markers are ordinary characters); (2) whitespace-only section names were accepted when spelled `[\"   \"]`; (3) control characters were rejected in section names although the spec states that rule for keys only. The second audit confirmed all three fixes with its own probes and no regressions.\n\n## Remaining caveats\n\n- Documents outside the dialect cannot round-trip because the dialect has no spelling for them (an entirely blank section name, or a key beginning with `;`, `#`, `[`); this is documented in the printer and README, and `parse` never produces such documents.\n- `[section] ; note` is rejected: the spec's grammar ends a header line after `]` plus whitespace.\n- `moon fmt --check` reports only the protected `ini_spec.mbt` (its deprecated `derive(...)` spelling), left untouched on purpose; `moon.pkg` was left as scaffolded.\n"
        }
